  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/EB23BC">Example <span data-tag="EB23BC">5.2.8.9</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be an $\infty $-category. Then $\calC $ admits a factorization system $(S_ L, S_ R)$, where $S_ L$ is the collection of all equivalences in $\calC $, and $S_ R$ consists of all morphisms of $\calC $. </p>
